                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="text">
                    <h3>Why do I have to complete this?</h3>
                    <p>This CAPTCHA proves that you are a real, breathing, human and allows you to continue accessing the website. This page allows us to ensure the security and safety of the website.</p>
                    <h3>Why do I keep getting this?</h3>
                    <p>You may have an extension on your browser that could interrupt the CAPTCHA process. If you’re consistently getting asked to complete this CAPTCHA, please try to disable your web browser extensions before completing the CAPTCHA.</p>
                    <p> Security &amp; Performance provided by <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20230302104438/https://nexuspipe.com/">NexusPIPE</a>. </p>
                    <br>
                    <br>
                </div>
            </div>
        </main>
        <main id="main_challenge" style="display: none; text-align: center;">
            <img class="ring" src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="NexusPIPE Ring" style="height: 128px"/>
            <h1>Please wait <span id="dots"></span>
            </h1>
            <p>We're doing a security check - this should only take a few seconds</p>
            <footer style="position: fixed; bottom: 0; left: 50vw; transform: translate(-50%, 0);">
                <p style="margin: 0 0; margin-bottom: -0.5em"> If this process does not complete automatically, please <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20230302104438/mailto:contact@nexuspipe.com">contact us</a>. </p>
                <p> Security &amp; Performance provided by <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20230302104438/https://nexuspipe.com/">NexusPIPE</a>. </p>
            </footer>
        </main>
        <script>
            document.querySelector("#domainMessage1").innerText = `Please complete the security check to access ${document.domain}`;
            setInterval(() => {
                document.querySelector('#dots').innerHTML += '.';
                if (document.querySelector('#dots').innerHTML.length >= 4) document.querySelector('#dots').innerHTML = '';
            }, 1000);
        </script>
